IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `epbc-claims-dates`

-- Environment Protection and Biodiversity Conservation Act 1999 (Cth) -- the questions of the person who wants to bring
-- a claim about a contravention of the Act: an injunction (Part 17 Division 14), judicial review of a decision made
-- under the Act (Part 17 Division 16), and compensation for loss or damage caused by a contravention (Part 18).
--
-- SEAT: the individual: an Australian citizen or resident whose interests are affected by conduct under the Act, or who
-- works for the protection or conservation of, or research into, the environment; a person acting on behalf of an
-- environmental organisation; a landholder bound by a conservation agreement; a person who suffered loss or damage from
-- a contravention. "Can I apply for an injunction?", "Can my group?", "What can the court order?", "Can I seek judicial
-- review?", "Can I recover my loss, and how much?". The Federal Court, the CEO, the Director and the Minister get no
-- seat: their findings and decisions are asked as facts.
--
-- Every exported question takes plain facts (yes/no, a number, a date, a choice from a list). No question takes a
-- DEONTIC or an EVENT. The provisions encoded set no deadline the claimant must meet (the time limits for judicial review
-- and for recovering a debt are in other Acts, not deposited), so there is no regulative rule here (NOTES.md).
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: ss 475, 476 (with s 307), 477, 479, 480A(5) (by its effect), 487, 488, 499(3), 500. Out, with
-- reasons, in NOTES.md.
--
-- Edition: Environment Protection and Biodiversity Conservation Act 1999, Compilation No. 70, compilation date 24 August
-- 2026 (includes amendments to Act No. 68, 2025; register id C2026C00369), deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00485.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026).
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation, Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. Whether conduct is an offence or other contravention, whether
-- interests are affected, whether activities are "a series of activities" for the environment, whether an expense was
-- "reasonably incurred" and whether loss "arises from" a contravention are for the court: they are INPUTS and the answer
-- is conditional on them. Answers follow the rulings on negatives of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 (NOTES.md): an answer
-- that is the text's own no is marked "(the text's no)"; an answer where the text is limited by its own wording or
-- silent is marked "NOTHING-kind".

§ `EPBC Act 1999: the questions of the person bringing a claim`

§§ `s 475 -- Injunctions for contravention of the Act: am I an interested person?`

-- s 475(6): "For the purposes of an application for an injunction relating to conduct or proposed conduct, an individual
-- is an interested person if the individual is an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident in Australia or an external
-- Territory, and: (a) the individual's interests have been, are or would be affected by the conduct or proposed conduct;
-- or (b) the individual engaged in a series of activities for protection or conservation of, or research into, the
-- environment at any time in the 2 years immediately before: (i) the conduct; or (ii) in the case of proposed
-- conduct--making the application for the injunction."
-- s 528: "interested person has the meaning given by section 475." The definition is closed and introduced by "if": when
-- it fails, the answer is the text's no.
-- (b) does not require the activities to be in Australia; s 487(2)(b) does (finding 2).

-- The day the 2 years run back from: the conduct, or for proposed conduct the making of the application.
GIVEN `the conduct is only proposed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE, `the day of the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 475 -- the day the 2 years end` `the conduct is only proposed` `the day of the conduct` `the day of the application` MEANS
    IF `the conduct is only proposed` THEN `the day of the application` ELSE `the day of the conduct`

DECLARE `Am I an interested person` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you are an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident, and your interests have been, are or would be affected by the conduct (s 475(6)(a))`
    `yes: you are an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident, and you engaged in a series of activities for the environment in the 2 years immediately before the conduct or, for proposed conduct, the application (s 475(6)(b))`
    `no: you are neither an Australian citizen nor ordinarily resident in Australia or an external Territory (s 475(6), the text's no)`
    `no: your interests are not affected and you have not engaged in a series of activities for the environment (s 475(6), the text's no)`
    `no: your interests are not affected and your last activity for the environment was outside the 2 years immediately before the conduct or, for proposed conduct, the application (s 475(6)(b), the text's no)`

@export Am I an interested person who may seek an injunction about conduct that contravenes the EPBC Act (s 475(6))? I must be an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident in Australia or an external Territory, and either my interests are affected by the conduct, or I engaged in a series of activities for the protection or conservation of, or research into, the environment in the 2 years before the conduct (or, for proposed conduct, before my application).
GIVEN `citizen or resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen, or ordinarily resident in Australia or an external Territory
      `my interests are affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your interests have been, are or would be affected by the conduct or proposed conduct
      `I engaged in a series of activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have engaged in a series of activities for the protection or conservation of, or research into, the environment (anywhere)
      `my last activity day` IS A DATE @desc The most recent day on which you carried on that series of activities (any day if none)
      `the conduct is only proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct has not happened yet and is only proposed
      `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day of the conduct you are applying about (for continuing conduct, the day of it you rely on; any day if the conduct is only proposed)
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE @desc The day you make, or will make, the application to the Federal Court
GIVETH AN `Am I an interested person`
`s 475(6) -- am I an interested person` `citizen or resident` `my interests are affected` `I engaged in a series of activities` `my last activity day` `the conduct is only proposed` `the day of the conduct` `the day of the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `citizen or resident`)
        THEN `no: you are neither an Australian citizen nor ordinarily resident in Australia or an external Territory (s 475(6), the text's no)`
        IF `my interests are affected`
        THEN `yes: you are an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident, and your interests have been, are or would be affected by the conduct (s 475(6)(a))`
        IF (NOT `I engaged in a series of activities`)
        THEN `no: your interests are not affected and you have not engaged in a series of activities for the environment (s 475(6), the text's no)`
        IF `my last activity day` `falls in the 2 years immediately before` `the end day`
        THEN `yes: you are an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident, and you engaged in a series of activities for the environment in the 2 years immediately before the conduct or, for proposed conduct, the application (s 475(6)(b))`
        OTHERWISE `no: your interests are not affected and your last activity for the environment was outside the 2 years immediately before the conduct or, for proposed conduct, the application (s 475(6)(b), the text's no)`
    WHERE
        `the end day` MEANS `s 475 -- the day the 2 years end` `the conduct is only proposed` `the day of the conduct` `the day of the application`

GIVEN a IS AN `Am I an interested person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 475(6) -- the answer is yes` a IF
        a EQUALS `yes: you are an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident, and your interests have been, are or would be affected by the conduct (s 475(6)(a))`
    OR  a EQUALS `yes: you are an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident, and you engaged in a series of activities for the environment in the 2 years immediately before the conduct or, for proposed conduct, the application (s 475(6)(b))`

§§ `s 475(1) -- Can I apply to the Federal Court for an injunction?`

-- s 475(1): "If a person has engaged, engages or proposes to engage in conduct consisting of an act or omission that
-- constitutes an offence or other contravention of this Act or the regulations: (a) the CEO; or (aa) if the conduct
-- relates to a Commonwealth reserve or a conservation zone--the Director; or (b) an interested person (other than an
-- unincorporated organisation); or (c) a person acting on behalf of an unincorporated organisation that is an interested
-- person; may apply to the Federal Court for an injunction."
-- The opening "If" is a condition: when the conduct is no contravention, s 475 gives no injunction (the text's no).
-- The list of applicants is not closed with "only": an individual who is not an interested person is outside the grant,
-- and the answer is NOTHING-kind (the Federal Court's other powers are saved by s 480).

DECLARE `Can I apply for an injunction` IS ONE OF
    `yes: as an interested person you may apply to the Federal Court for an injunction (s 475(1)(b))`
    `no: the conduct is not an offence or other contravention of the Act or the regulations, so s 475 gives no injunction (s 475(1), the text's no)`
    `not shown: you are not an interested person, and s 475(1) gives standing only to the persons it names; other remedies are outside this encoding (s 475(1), NOTHING-kind)`

@export Can I apply to the Federal Court for an injunction against conduct that contravenes the EPBC Act (s 475(1))? The conduct must be an offence or other contravention of the Act or the regulations, and I must be an interested person.
GIVEN `the conduct contravenes the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct (done, being done or proposed) is, or would be, an offence or other contravention of the EPBC Act or its regulations, as the court would find
      `citizen or resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen, or ordinarily resident in Australia or an external Territory
      `my interests are affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your interests have been, are or would be affected by the conduct or proposed conduct
      `I engaged in a series of activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have engaged in a series of activities for the protection or conservation of, or research into, the environment (anywhere)
      `my last activity day` IS A DATE @desc The most recent day on which you carried on that series of activities (any day if none)
      `the conduct is only proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct has not happened yet and is only proposed
      `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day of the conduct you are applying about (for continuing conduct, the day of it you rely on; any day if the conduct is only proposed)
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE @desc The day you make, or will make, the application to the Federal Court
GIVETH A `Can I apply for an injunction`
`s 475(1) -- can I apply for an injunction` `the conduct contravenes the Act` `citizen or resident` `my interests are affected` `I engaged in a series of activities` `my last activity day` `the conduct is only proposed` `the day of the conduct` `the day of the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the conduct contravenes the Act`)
        THEN `no: the conduct is not an offence or other contravention of the Act or the regulations, so s 475 gives no injunction (s 475(1), the text's no)`
        IF `s 475(6) -- the answer is yes` (`s 475(6) -- am I an interested person` `citizen or resident` `my interests are affected` `I engaged in a series of activities` `my last activity day` `the conduct is only proposed` `the day of the conduct` `the day of the application`)
        THEN `yes: as an interested person you may apply to the Federal Court for an injunction (s 475(1)(b))`
        OTHERWISE `not shown: you are not an interested person, and s 475(1) gives standing only to the persons it names; other remedies are outside this encoding (s 475(1), NOTHING-kind)`

§§ `s 475(7) -- Can my organisation apply, or can I apply on its behalf?`

-- s 475(7): "an organisation (whether incorporated or not) is an interested person if it is incorporated (or was otherwise
-- established) in Australia or an external Territory and one or more of the following conditions are met: (a) the
-- organisation's interests have been, are or would be affected by the conduct or proposed conduct; (b) if the
-- application relates to conduct--at any time during the 2 years immediately before the conduct: (i) the organisation's
-- objects or purposes included the protection or conservation of, or research into, the environment; and (ii) the
-- organisation engaged in a series of activities related to [that]; (c) if the application relates to proposed
-- conduct--at any time during the 2 years immediately before the making of the application: [the same (i) and (ii)]."
-- (i) and (ii) are read as holding together, at some time in the 2 years (fork F5): the person gives the last day on
-- which the organisation carried on its activities while its objects included the environment.
-- s 475(1)(b) lets an incorporated organisation apply itself; (c) lets "a person acting on behalf of an unincorporated
-- organisation that is an interested person" apply.

DECLARE `Can my organisation apply for an injunction` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the organisation is an interested person and, being incorporated, may itself apply to the Federal Court for an injunction (s 475(1)(b), (7))`
    `yes: the organisation is an interested person and, being unincorporated, a person acting on its behalf (such as you) may apply to the Federal Court for an injunction (s 475(1)(c), (7))`
    `no: the conduct is not an offence or other contravention of the Act or the regulations, so s 475 gives the organisation no injunction (s 475(1), the text's no)`
    `no: the organisation is not incorporated or otherwise established in Australia or an external Territory, so it is not an interested person (s 475(7), the text's no)`
    `no: the organisation's interests are not affected, and it did not have environmental objects and carry on a series of environmental activities in the 2 years immediately before the conduct or, for proposed conduct, the application (s 475(7), the text's no)`

@export Can my organisation apply to the Federal Court for an injunction against conduct that contravenes the EPBC Act, or can I apply on its behalf (s 475(1), (7))? The organisation must be incorporated or established in Australia or an external Territory, and either its interests are affected, or in the 2 years before the conduct (or the application, for proposed conduct) its objects included the environment and it carried on a series of environmental activities.
GIVEN `the conduct contravenes the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct (done, being done or proposed) is, or would be, an offence or other contravention of the EPBC Act or its regulations, as the court would find
      `established in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation is incorporated, or was otherwise established, in Australia or an external Territory
      `incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation is incorporated (answer no for an unincorporated association or group)
      `its interests are affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation's interests have been, are or would be affected by the conduct or proposed conduct
      `environmental objects and activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation has engaged in a series of activities for the protection or conservation of, or research into, the environment at a time when its objects or purposes included that
      `its last activity day` IS A DATE @desc The most recent day on which the organisation carried on those activities while its objects included the environment (any day if never)
      `the conduct is only proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct has not happened yet and is only proposed
      `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day of the conduct the application is about (for continuing conduct, the day of it relied on; any day if the conduct is only proposed)
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE @desc The day the application to the Federal Court is, or will be, made
GIVETH A `Can my organisation apply for an injunction`
`s 475(7) -- can my organisation apply for an injunction` `the conduct contravenes the Act` `established in Australia` `incorporated` `its interests are affected` `environmental objects and activities` `its last activity day` `the conduct is only proposed` `the day of the conduct` `the day of the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the conduct contravenes the Act`)
        THEN `no: the conduct is not an offence or other contravention of the Act or the regulations, so s 475 gives the organisation no injunction (s 475(1), the text's no)`
        IF (NOT `established in Australia`)
        THEN `no: the organisation is not incorporated or otherwise established in Australia or an external Territory, so it is not an interested person (s 475(7), the text's no)`
        IF (NOT `the organisation qualifies`)
        THEN `no: the organisation's interests are not affected, and it did not have environmental objects and carry on a series of environmental activities in the 2 years immediately before the conduct or, for proposed conduct, the application (s 475(7), the text's no)`
        IF `incorporated`
        THEN `yes: the organisation is an interested person and, being incorporated, may itself apply to the Federal Court for an injunction (s 475(1)(b), (7))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the organisation is an interested person and, being unincorporated, a person acting on its behalf (such as you) may apply to the Federal Court for an injunction (s 475(1)(c), (7))`
    WHERE
        `the end day` MEANS `s 475 -- the day the 2 years end` `the conduct is only proposed` `the day of the conduct` `the day of the application`
        `the organisation qualifies` MEANS
                `its interests are affected`
            OR  (    `environmental objects and activities`
                 AND `its last activity day` `falls in the 2 years immediately before` `the end day`)

§§ `ss 475(2)-(5), 477, 479, 480A -- What can the court order?`

-- s 475(2): "If a person has engaged, is engaging or is proposing to engage in conduct constituting an offence or other
-- contravention ..., the Court may grant an injunction restraining the person from engaging in the conduct."
-- (3): "If the court grants an injunction restraining a person from engaging in conduct and in the Court's opinion it is
-- desirable to do so, the Court may make an order requiring the person to do something (including repair or mitigate
-- damage to the environment)."
-- (4): "If a person has refused or failed, or is refusing or failing, or is proposing to refuse or fail to do an act, and
-- the refusal or failure did, does or would constitute an offence or other contravention ..., the Court may grant an
-- injunction requiring the person to do the act."
-- (5): "Before deciding an application for an injunction ..., the Court may grant an interim injunction".
-- s 479(1), (2): the Court may grant either kind "whether or not" the person intends to engage (or fail) again, has done
-- so before, or there is "a significant risk of injury or damage to human beings or the environment".
-- s 477: "On application, the Federal Court may discharge or vary an injunction."
-- s 480A(5): a remediation order may be applied for by "the CEO personally" or the Director personally; a private
-- applicant is not named (NOTHING-kind for the applicant; the s 475(3) order is the route open to the applicant).
-- "may" throughout: what the court may grant, never whether it will.

DECLARE `What the person did` IS ONE OF
    `engaged in an act`
    `is engaging in an act`
    `proposes to engage in an act`
    `refused or failed to do an act`
    `is refusing or failing to do an act`
    `proposes to refuse or fail to do an act`

DECLARE `What the court may order` IS ONE OF
    `the court may grant an injunction restraining the person from the conduct, and if it thinks it desirable order the person to do something, including repair or mitigate damage to the environment; it may grant an interim injunction before deciding; it need not find that the person intends to continue or did it before, or that there is a significant risk of injury or damage (ss 475(2), (3), (5), 479(1)); the injunction may later be discharged or varied on application (s 477); a remediation order under s 480A is for the CEO or the Director to seek`
    `the court may grant an injunction requiring the person to do the act; it may grant an interim injunction before deciding; it need not find that the person intends to refuse or fail again or did so before, or that there is a significant risk of injury or damage (ss 475(4), (5), 479(2)); the injunction may later be discharged or varied on application (s 477); a remediation order under s 480A is for the CEO or the Director to seek`
    `none under s 475: the conduct, refusal or failure is not an offence or other contravention of the Act or the regulations (s 475(2), (4), the text's no)`

@export What can the Federal Court order on my application for an injunction under the EPBC Act (ss 475(2)-(5), 477, 479)? It depends on whether the person did, is doing or proposes an act, or refused, is refusing or proposes to refuse or fail to do one, and whether that is a contravention of the Act.
GIVEN `what the person did` IS A `What the person did` @desc What the person you are applying against did, is doing or proposes: an act, or a refusal or failure to do an act
      `it contravenes the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act, refusal or failure is, or would be, an offence or other contravention of the EPBC Act or its regulations, as the court would find
GIVETH A `What the court may order`
`ss 475, 479 -- what can the court order` `what the person did` `it contravenes the Act` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it contravenes the Act`)
    THEN `none under s 475: the conduct, refusal or failure is not an offence or other contravention of the Act or the regulations (s 475(2), (4), the text's no)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `what the person did`
         WHEN `engaged in an act` THEN `the prohibitory orders`
         WHEN `is engaging in an act` THEN `the prohibitory orders`
         WHEN `proposes to engage in an act` THEN `the prohibitory orders`
         OTHERWISE `the mandatory orders`
    WHERE
        `the prohibitory orders` MEANS `the court may grant an injunction restraining the person from the conduct, and if it thinks it desirable order the person to do something, including repair or mitigate damage to the environment; it may grant an interim injunction before deciding; it need not find that the person intends to continue or did it before, or that there is a significant risk of injury or damage (ss 475(2), (3), (5), 479(1)); the injunction may later be discharged or varied on application (s 477); a remediation order under s 480A is for the CEO or the Director to seek`
        `the mandatory orders` MEANS `the court may grant an injunction requiring the person to do the act; it may grant an interim injunction before deciding; it need not find that the person intends to refuse or fail again or did so before, or that there is a significant risk of injury or damage (ss 475(4), (5), 479(2)); the injunction may later be discharged or varied on application (s 477); a remediation order under s 480A is for the CEO or the Director to seek`

§§ `s 476 -- Situation: I am bound by a conservation agreement. Can I get an injunction against another party?`

-- This group arises only for a person bound by a conservation agreement (s 305), typically a landholder.
-- s 307: "A conservation agreement is legally binding on: (a) the Commonwealth; and (b) the person or persons with whom
-- the Minister entered into the agreement on behalf of the Commonwealth; and (c) anyone else who is a successor to the
-- whole or any part of any interest that a person mentioned in paragraph (b) had, when the agreement was entered into,
-- in any place covered by the agreement."
-- s 476(1): "If a person bound by a conservation agreement engages or proposes to engage in conduct consisting of an act
-- or omission that constitutes a contravention of the agreement, any of the following persons may apply to the Federal
-- Court for an injunction: (a) another person bound by the agreement; (b) the CEO; (c) [the Director]."
-- (2)-(5) mirror s 475(2)-(5), with "contravening the agreement".
-- (1) speaks only of a person who "engages or proposes to engage"; (2) and (4) also reach one who "has engaged" or "has
-- refused or failed". Past conduct that has stopped is read as outside (1): NOTHING-kind (fork F4, finding 3).

DECLARE `How am I bound by the agreement` IS ONE OF
    `I entered into the agreement with the Minister`
    `I am a successor to an interest in a place the agreement covers`
    `I am not bound by the agreement`

DECLARE `When the other party acts` IS ONE OF
    `the other party is now acting or failing to act`
    `the other party proposes to act or fail to act`
    `the other party acted or failed to act in the past but has stopped`

DECLARE `Can I seek an injunction under the agreement` IS ONE OF
    `yes: as another person bound by the agreement you may apply to the Federal Court for an injunction; the court may restrain the conduct (with an order to repair or mitigate damage if desirable), order the party to do the act, or grant an interim injunction (s 476(1)(a), (2)-(5))`
    `no: the conduct is not a contravention of the conservation agreement (s 476(1), the text's no)`
    `no: the person acting is not bound by the conservation agreement (s 476(1), the text's no)`
    `not shown: you are not bound by the agreement, and s 476(1) gives standing only to another person bound, the CEO and the Director (NOTHING-kind)`
    `not shown: s 476(1) speaks of a party who engages or proposes to engage in the conduct; conduct that is wholly past is not within its words, though s 476(2) speaks of a party who has engaged (fork F4, NOTHING-kind)`

@export I am bound by a conservation agreement under the EPBC Act. Can I apply to the Federal Court for an injunction against another party to it who contravenes it (ss 307, 476)?
GIVEN `how I am bound` IS A `How am I bound by the agreement` @desc How you are bound by the conservation agreement: you entered into it with the Minister, or you succeeded to an interest in a place it covers that such a person had when it was made, or you are not bound
      `the other party is bound` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person whose conduct you complain of is bound by the agreement (the Commonwealth, a person who entered into it with the Minister, or a successor to an interest in a place it covers)
      `when` IS A `When the other party acts` @desc Whether the other party is now acting (or failing to act), proposes to, or did so only in the past and has stopped
      `it contravenes the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act or omission is, or would be, a contravention of the conservation agreement, as the court would find
GIVETH A `Can I seek an injunction under the agreement`
`s 476 -- can I seek an injunction under the agreement` `how I am bound` `the other party is bound` `when` `it contravenes the agreement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `it contravenes the agreement`)
        THEN `no: the conduct is not a contravention of the conservation agreement (s 476(1), the text's no)`
        IF (NOT `the other party is bound`)
        THEN `no: the person acting is not bound by the conservation agreement (s 476(1), the text's no)`
        IF `how I am bound` EQUALS `I am not bound by the agreement`
        THEN `not shown: you are not bound by the agreement, and s 476(1) gives standing only to another person bound, the CEO and the Director (NOTHING-kind)`
        IF `when` EQUALS `the other party acted or failed to act in the past but has stopped`
        THEN `not shown: s 476(1) speaks of a party who engages or proposes to engage in the conduct; conduct that is wholly past is not within its words, though s 476(2) speaks of a party who has engaged (fork F4, NOTHING-kind)`
        OTHERWISE `yes: as another person bound by the agreement you may apply to the Federal Court for an injunction; the court may restrain the conduct (with an order to repair or mitigate damage if desirable), order the party to do the act, or grant an interim injunction (s 476(1)(a), (2)-(5))`

§§ `ss 487, 488 -- Can I seek judicial review of a decision under the Act?`

-- s 487(1): "This section extends (and does not limit) the meaning of the term person aggrieved in the Administrative
-- Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977 for the purposes of the application of that Act in relation to: (a) a decision
-- made under this Act or the regulations; or (b) a failure to make a decision ...; or (c) conduct engaged in for the
-- purpose of making a decision ...".
-- (2): "An individual is taken to be a person aggrieved by the decision, failure or conduct if: (a) the individual is an
-- Australian citizen or ordinarily resident in Australia or an external Territory; and (b) at any time in the 2 years
-- immediately before the decision, failure or conduct, the individual has engaged in a series of activities in
-- Australia or an external Territory for protection or conservation of, or research into, the environment."
-- Because s 487 "does not limit" the ADJR Act's own meaning (a person whose interests are adversely affected), a person
-- who fails s 487(2) may still be a person aggrieved: the answer is NOTHING-kind, never no. The ADJR Act is not
-- deposited; its own test and its time limits are not encoded.

DECLARE `Am I a person aggrieved` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you are taken to be a person aggrieved by the decision, failure or conduct, and may apply for review under the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977 (s 487(2))`
    `not shown by s 487: you are not an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident; you may still be a person aggrieved under the ADJR Act's own meaning, which s 487 extends and does not limit (s 487(1), NOTHING-kind)`
    `not shown by s 487: you have not engaged in a series of environmental activities in Australia or an external Territory; you may still be a person aggrieved under the ADJR Act's own meaning (s 487(1), NOTHING-kind)`
    `not shown by s 487: your last environmental activity was outside the 2 years immediately before the decision, failure or conduct; you may still be a person aggrieved under the ADJR Act's own meaning (s 487(1), NOTHING-kind)`

@export Am I taken to be a person aggrieved, so that I can seek judicial review of a decision (or a failure to decide, or conduct for making a decision) under the EPBC Act (s 487(2))? I must be an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident, and have engaged in a series of activities in Australia for the protection or conservation of, or research into, the environment in the 2 years before the decision.
GIVEN `citizen or resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen, or ordinarily resident in Australia or an external Territory
      `I engaged in activities in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have engaged in a series of activities in Australia or an external Territory for the protection or conservation of, or research into, the environment
      `my last activity day` IS A DATE @desc The most recent day on which you carried on that series of activities in Australia or an external Territory (any day if none)
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day of the decision, the failure to decide, or the conduct for the purpose of making a decision, that you want reviewed
GIVETH AN `Am I a person aggrieved`
`s 487(2) -- am I a person aggrieved` `citizen or resident` `I engaged in activities in Australia` `my last activity day` `the day of the decision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `citizen or resident`)
        THEN `not shown by s 487: you are not an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident; you may still be a person aggrieved under the ADJR Act's own meaning, which s 487 extends and does not limit (s 487(1), NOTHING-kind)`
        IF (NOT `I engaged in activities in Australia`)
        THEN `not shown by s 487: you have not engaged in a series of environmental activities in Australia or an external Territory; you may still be a person aggrieved under the ADJR Act's own meaning (s 487(1), NOTHING-kind)`
        IF `my last activity day` `falls in the 2 years immediately before` `the day of the decision`
        THEN `yes: you are taken to be a person aggrieved by the decision, failure or conduct, and may apply for review under the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977 (s 487(2))`
        OTHERWISE `not shown by s 487: your last environmental activity was outside the 2 years immediately before the decision, failure or conduct; you may still be a person aggrieved under the ADJR Act's own meaning (s 487(1), NOTHING-kind)`

-- s 487(3): "An organisation or association (whether incorporated or not) is taken to be a person aggrieved ... if:
-- (a) the organisation or association is incorporated, or was otherwise established, in Australia or an external
-- Territory; and (b) at any time in the 2 years immediately before the decision, failure or conduct, the organisation or
-- association has engaged in a series of activities in Australia or an external Territory for protection or
-- conservation of, or research into, the environment; and (c) at the time of the decision, failure or conduct, the
-- objects or purposes of the organisation or association included protection or conservation of, or research into, the
-- environment."
-- s 488(1): "A person acting on behalf of an unincorporated organisation that is a person aggrieved ... may apply under
-- that Act for a review"; (2): the ADJR Act "applies in relation to the person as if he or she were a person aggrieved".
-- Unlike s 475(7), the objects test is at the time of the decision, and there is no "interests affected" limb (the ADJR
-- Act's own meaning covers that) (finding 4).

DECLARE `Can my organisation seek review` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the organisation is taken to be a person aggrieved and, being incorporated, may itself apply for review under the ADJR Act (s 487(3))`
    `yes: the organisation is taken to be a person aggrieved and, being unincorporated, a person acting on its behalf (such as you) may apply for review, as if a person aggrieved (ss 487(3), 488)`
    `not shown by s 487: the organisation does not meet s 487(3); it may still be a person aggrieved under the ADJR Act's own meaning, and if it is and is unincorporated, a person acting on its behalf may apply (ss 487(1), 488, NOTHING-kind)`

@export Can my organisation seek judicial review of a decision under the EPBC Act, or can I apply on its behalf (ss 487(3), 488)? The organisation must be incorporated or established in Australia, have engaged in a series of environmental activities in Australia in the 2 years before the decision, and have environmental objects at the time of the decision.
GIVEN `established in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation or association is incorporated, or was otherwise established, in Australia or an external Territory
      `incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation or association is incorporated (answer no for an unincorporated association or group)
      `it engaged in activities in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation has engaged in a series of activities in Australia or an external Territory for the protection or conservation of, or research into, the environment
      `its last activity day` IS A DATE @desc The most recent day on which the organisation carried on that series of activities (any day if none)
      `environmental objects at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the decision, failure or conduct, the organisation's objects or purposes included the protection or conservation of, or research into, the environment
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day of the decision, the failure to decide, or the conduct for the purpose of making a decision, to be reviewed
GIVETH A `Can my organisation seek review`
`ss 487(3), 488 -- can my organisation seek review` `established in Australia` `incorporated` `it engaged in activities in Australia` `its last activity day` `environmental objects at the time` `the day of the decision` MEANS
    IF      `established in Australia`
        AND `it engaged in activities in Australia`
        AND `its last activity day` `falls in the 2 years immediately before` `the day of the decision`
        AND `environmental objects at the time`
    THEN IF `incorporated`
         THEN `yes: the organisation is taken to be a person aggrieved and, being incorporated, may itself apply for review under the ADJR Act (s 487(3))`
         ELSE `yes: the organisation is taken to be a person aggrieved and, being unincorporated, a person acting on its behalf (such as you) may apply for review, as if a person aggrieved (ss 487(3), 488)`
    ELSE `not shown by s 487: the organisation does not meet s 487(3); it may still be a person aggrieved under the ADJR Act's own meaning, and if it is and is unincorporated, a person acting on its behalf may apply (ss 487(1), 488, NOTHING-kind)`

§§ `s 500 -- Situation: I suffered loss or damage from a contravention. Can I recover it?`

-- This group arises only for a person who has suffered loss or damage.
-- s 500(1): "A person (the wrongdoer) who contravenes this Act or the regulations is liable to pay to another person (the
-- affected party) who suffers loss or damage arising from the contravention an amount equal to the other person's loss
-- or damage."
-- (3): "An amount payable under subsection (1) is a debt due to the affected party, recoverable in a court of competent
-- jurisdiction." (6): it applies "whether or not the contravention was an offence" and "whether or not the provision
-- contravened is a civil penalty provision" (no input).
-- (7): "This section does not apply to a decision (or a failure to make a decision or conduct for the purposes of making
-- a decision) purportedly under this Act or the regulations that contravenes this Act or the regulations." A flat
-- negative: the text's no.
-- s 499(3): where "(a) a person provided false or misleading information in contravention of section 489; and (b) as a
-- result of the contravention the Minister or the CEO granted an environmental authority to a person, or set conditions
-- ..., unaware of the certainty or likelihood of the action covered by the authority: (i) resulting in damage to the
-- environment or to a matter protected by a provision of Part 3; or (ii) giving rise to a condition relating to [either];
-- and (c) the action results in damage to the environment or gives rise to a condition relating to the environment;
-- then, for the purposes of this section and section 500, the damage or condition is taken to arise from the provision
-- of false or misleading information in contravention of section 489."
-- No contravention, or loss not arising from one: s 500 is silent about the case (a scope limit with no "only"), so
-- NOTHING-kind (fork F6); s 501 saves other rights.

DECLARE `Can I recover my loss` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the person who contravened the Act is liable to pay you an amount equal to your loss or damage; it is a debt due to you, recoverable in a court of competent jurisdiction (s 500(1), (3))`
    `yes: the damage or condition is taken to arise from the false or misleading information given in contravention of s 489, so the person who gave it is liable to pay you an amount equal to your loss or damage arising from it, as a debt recoverable in a court of competent jurisdiction (ss 499(3), 500(1), (3))`
    `no: s 500 does not apply to a decision, a failure to make a decision, or conduct for the purposes of making a decision, purportedly under the Act (s 500(7), the text's no)`
    `not shown: no contravention of the Act or the regulations is established, and s 500 is silent about such a case (s 500(1), NOTHING-kind)`
    `not shown: your loss or damage is not shown to arise from the contravention, and s 500 is silent about such a case (s 500(1), NOTHING-kind)`

@export I suffered loss or damage. Can I recover it from the person who contravened the EPBC Act (ss 499(3), 500)? A person who contravenes the Act or the regulations must pay an amount equal to the loss or damage arising from the contravention. Damage from an approval obtained by false or misleading information is taken to arise from giving that information.
GIVEN `it is a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you complain of is a decision, a failure to make a decision, or conduct for the purposes of making a decision, purportedly under the EPBC Act (for example the grant of an approval itself)
      `they contravened the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person contravened the EPBC Act or its regulations (an offence, a civil penalty provision or any other provision), as the court would find
      `my loss arose from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered loss or damage arising from that contravention, as the court would find
      `they gave false information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person gave false or misleading information to obtain an approval or permit, in contravention of section 489
      `the authority was granted unaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as a result, the Minister or the CEO granted the approval or permit, or set its conditions, unaware that the action it covers would or was likely to damage the environment or a matter protected by Part 3
      `the action damaged the environment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action covered by the approval or permit has damaged the environment or given rise to a condition relating to the environment
      `my loss arose from that damage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered loss or damage arising from that damage or condition, as the court would find
GIVETH A `Can I recover my loss`
`s 500 -- can I recover my loss` `it is a decision` `they contravened the Act` `my loss arose from it` `they gave false information` `the authority was granted unaware` `the action damaged the environment` `my loss arose from that damage` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a decision`
        THEN `no: s 500 does not apply to a decision, a failure to make a decision, or conduct for the purposes of making a decision, purportedly under the Act (s 500(7), the text's no)`
        IF `they contravened the Act` AND `my loss arose from it`
        THEN `yes: the person who contravened the Act is liable to pay you an amount equal to your loss or damage; it is a debt due to you, recoverable in a court of competent jurisdiction (s 500(1), (3))`
        IF `the s 499(3) deeming applies` AND `my loss arose from that damage`
        THEN `yes: the damage or condition is taken to arise from the false or misleading information given in contravention of s 489, so the person who gave it is liable to pay you an amount equal to your loss or damage arising from it, as a debt recoverable in a court of competent jurisdiction (ss 499(3), 500(1), (3))`
        IF `they contravened the Act` OR `they gave false information`
        THEN `not shown: your loss or damage is not shown to arise from the contravention, and s 500 is silent about such a case (s 500(1), NOTHING-kind)`
        OTHERWISE `not shown: no contravention of the Act or the regulations is established, and s 500 is silent about such a case (s 500(1), NOTHING-kind)`
    WHERE
        `the s 499(3) deeming applies` MEANS `they gave false information` AND `the authority was granted unaware` AND `the action damaged the environment`

-- s 500(1): "an amount equal to the other person's loss or damage". (2): "Without limiting the amount payable under
-- subsection (1), the loss or damage a person suffers ... includes the expenses and liabilities (if any) reasonably
-- incurred by the affected party to: (a) repair or remove any condition that arises from the act or omission ...;
-- (b) mitigate any damage that arises from [it] ...; (c) prevent any damage likely to arise from [it]", each relating to
-- the environment or, for a Part 3 contravention, the matter protected.
-- "reasonably incurred" is the court's judgment: the person gives the amounts the court accepts as reasonably incurred.
-- The other loss and the (2) expenses are separate amounts (no double counting); the total is their sum.

@export How much am I owed under s 500 by a person liable for my loss or damage from a contravention of the EPBC Act? An amount equal to my loss or damage, including the expenses and liabilities I reasonably incurred to repair or remove a resulting condition, to mitigate damage, or to prevent likely damage (s 500(1), (2)).
GIVEN `my other loss` IS A NUMBER @desc Your loss or damage arising from the contravention, in dollars, other than the expenses and liabilities asked below
      `repair or removal costs` IS A NUMBER @desc Expenses and liabilities, in dollars, you reasonably incurred to repair or remove a condition arising from the contravention that relates to the environment (or the matter protected by Part 3)
      `mitigation costs` IS A NUMBER @desc Expenses and liabilities, in dollars, you reasonably incurred to mitigate damage arising from the contravention to the environment (or the matter protected by Part 3)
      `prevention costs` IS A NUMBER @desc Expenses and liabilities, in dollars, you reasonably incurred to prevent damage likely to arise from the contravention to the environment (or the matter protected by Part 3)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 500(1), (2) -- how much am I owed` `my other loss` `repair or removal costs` `mitigation costs` `prevention costs` MEANS
    `my other loss` PLUS `repair or removal costs` PLUS `mitigation costs` PLUS `prevention costs`

-- s 500(4): "If 2 or more persons are liable under subsection (1) to pay an amount in respect of the same loss or damage,
-- those persons are jointly and severally liable to pay the sum."

DECLARE `Whom can I recover from` IS ONE OF
    `the one person liable must pay you the whole amount (s 500(1))`
    `the persons liable are jointly and severally liable: you may recover the whole sum from any one of them, or from them together, but not more than the sum in all (s 500(4))`
    `not shown: no person is liable to you under s 500(1) on these facts (NOTHING-kind)`

@export More than one person may be liable for my loss or damage from a contravention of the EPBC Act. Can I recover the whole amount from any one of them (s 500(4))?
GIVEN `how many are liable` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons are liable under s 500(1) to pay you an amount for the same loss or damage
GIVETH A `Whom can I recover from`
`s 500(4) -- whom can I recover from` `how many are liable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `how many are liable` AT LEAST 2
        THEN `the persons liable are jointly and severally liable: you may recover the whole sum from any one of them, or from them together, but not more than the sum in all (s 500(4))`
        IF `how many are liable` EQUALS 1
        THEN `the one person liable must pay you the whole amount (s 500(1))`
        OTHERWISE `not shown: no person is liable to you under s 500(1) on these facts (NOTHING-kind)`

-- s 500(5): "A finding by a court in criminal proceedings or civil proceedings that the wrongdoer contravened this Act or
-- the regulations is admissible as evidence of that fact in proceedings to recover an amount payable under subsection
-- (1)." Admissible, not conclusive. Without such a finding the text is silent: NOTHING-kind.

DECLARE `Can I use the earlier finding` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the court's finding in the criminal or civil proceedings that the wrongdoer contravened the Act or the regulations is admissible as evidence of the contravention in your proceedings to recover (admissible, not conclusive) (s 500(5))`
    `not shown: there is no earlier court finding that the wrongdoer contravened the Act or the regulations; s 500(5) does not help, and the contravention must be proved (NOTHING-kind)`

@export In my claim to recover loss or damage under s 500 of the EPBC Act, can I rely on an earlier court finding that the wrongdoer contravened the Act (s 500(5))?
GIVEN `a court found the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court, in criminal proceedings (a conviction) or civil proceedings (such as a civil penalty or injunction case), found that the wrongdoer contravened the EPBC Act or its regulations
GIVETH A `Can I use the earlier finding`
`s 500(5) -- can I use the earlier finding` `a court found the contravention` MEANS
    IF `a court found the contravention`
    THEN `yes: the court's finding in the criminal or civil proceedings that the wrongdoer contravened the Act or the regulations is admissible as evidence of the contravention in your proceedings to recover (admissible, not conclusive) (s 500(5))`
    ELSE `not shown: there is no earlier court finding that the wrongdoer contravened the Act or the regulations; s 500(5) does not help, and the contravention must be proved (NOTHING-kind)`
